1
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,886
Captioning made possible
by Lions Gate Entertainment

2
00:01:59,625 --> 00:02:02,336
Subject's name is John Kramer.

3
00:02:02,378 --> 00:02:06,674
A 52-year-old male, caucasian.

4
00:02:07,633 --> 00:02:08,884
He's seen better days.

5
00:02:43,794 --> 00:02:46,672
<i>We have a recent rectangular transaction</i>

6
00:02:46,714 --> 00:02:48,841
<i>to the left occipital.</i>

7
00:02:50,092 --> 00:02:51,760
<i>Some kind of backdoor brain surgery.</i>

8
00:04:23,143 --> 00:04:25,062
<i>Let's check the stomach.</i>

9
00:04:44,331 --> 00:04:46,333
<i>What the hell?</i>

10
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:50,546
Get homicide here, now.

11
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,140
Where is it?

12
00:05:02,141 --> 00:05:03,726
It was in his stomach.

13
00:05:05,185 --> 00:05:06,562
Cut it out.

14
00:05:39,803 --> 00:05:41,722
<i>Are you there, detective?</i>

15
00:05:41,764 --> 00:05:46,643
<i>If so, you are</i>
<i>probably the last man standing.</i>

16
00:05:46,685 --> 00:05:49,521
<i>Now perhaps, you will succeed,</i>

17
00:05:49,563 --> 00:05:51,273
<i>where the others have failed.</i>

18
00:05:51,315 --> 00:05:54,943
<i>You think you will walk away untested?</i>

19
00:05:54,985 --> 00:05:58,822
<i>I promise that my work will continue.</i>

20
00:05:58,864 --> 00:06:02,284
<i>You think it's over just because I'm dead?</i>

21
00:06:02,326 --> 00:06:07,206
It's not over. The games have just begun.

22
00:06:19,009 --> 00:06:22,763
What the fuck? What the fuck?

23
00:06:26,225 --> 00:06:27,434
My eyes!

24
00:06:28,352 --> 00:06:30,312
My eyes. Fuck.

25
00:06:31,605 --> 00:06:33,524
What the fuck is it?

26
00:06:43,826 --> 00:06:44,743
Who's there?

27
00:06:46,453 --> 00:06:49,373
Talk to me! What
are you doing? Talk to me!

28
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,931
Talk to me!

29
00:07:12,521 --> 00:07:13,480
Stop it!

30
00:07:15,941 --> 00:07:17,151
Stop!

31
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:19,153
Uh!

32
00:07:24,241 --> 00:07:26,243
Stop it! Stop it!

33
00:07:48,265 --> 00:07:51,727
<i>What are you doing to</i>
<i>me? What are you doing?</i>

34
00:07:51,768 --> 00:07:54,062
<i>What are you doing? Help!</i>

35
00:07:54,104 --> 00:07:55,105
<i>Help!</i>

36
00:07:55,939 --> 00:07:57,858
<i>Who's doing this to me?!</i>

37
00:08:05,449 --> 00:08:06,700
Aah!

38
00:08:13,373 --> 00:08:14,625
Stay away from me!

39
00:08:20,172 --> 00:08:22,257
What'd I do?!

40
00:08:49,034 --> 00:08:50,327
Get off me!

41
00:08:51,203 --> 00:08:52,287
Ah!

42
00:08:52,329 --> 00:08:53,330
Get off me!

43
00:09:50,721 --> 00:09:53,098
<i>-Right side clear.</i>
<i>-Left side clear.</i>

44
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:54,641
Clear.

45
00:09:58,353 --> 00:09:59,313
<i>In position.</i>

46
00:10:00,522 --> 00:10:02,649
-<i>Standing by.</i>
-Hold right there.

47
00:10:05,110 --> 00:10:06,528
<i>I see movement.</i>

48
00:10:11,366 --> 00:10:12,534
We have a device.

49
00:10:13,493 --> 00:10:16,079
-You get eyes in there before you go in.
-Get some eyes in here.

50
00:10:17,039 --> 00:10:18,290
Moving now.

51
00:10:35,265 --> 00:10:36,516
Doorway's clear.

52
00:11:12,719 --> 00:11:15,222
-It's Kerry!
-<i>Rigg! Rigg, don't! Don't do it!</i>

53
00:11:15,263 --> 00:11:17,182
-We're not secure!
-Rigg, I said don't!

54
00:11:18,058 --> 00:11:19,101
Stop him!

55
00:11:19,142 --> 00:11:21,395
Do not go through that door!

56
00:11:21,436 --> 00:11:23,105
Kerry!

57
00:11:23,772 --> 00:11:25,315
Shit.

58
00:11:48,755 --> 00:11:50,590
Give me the coroner's office.

59
00:11:50,674 --> 00:11:53,510
- <i> Copy.</i>
- Somebody get those rats off her.

60
00:11:58,723 --> 00:12:00,600
<i>Just get the light on it.</i>

61
00:12:04,229 --> 00:12:05,355
Cut her down.

62
00:12:06,148 --> 00:12:07,899
You know I can't do that.

63
00:12:10,444 --> 00:12:12,195
I said, cut her down.

64
00:12:13,822 --> 00:12:14,990
Please.

65
00:12:22,789 --> 00:12:24,541
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

66
00:12:25,959 --> 00:12:28,879
You know never to go
through an unsecured door. Ever.

67
00:12:29,212 --> 00:12:30,839
I thought she was still alive.

68
00:12:31,256 --> 00:12:33,508
<i>Thought I could save her.</i>

69
00:12:34,885 --> 00:12:36,636
Did you ever think we'd end up here

70
00:12:37,220 --> 00:12:39,222
<i>when we first started?</i>

71
00:12:40,432 --> 00:12:41,516
No.

72
00:12:42,434 --> 00:12:46,188
<i>Didn't see it happening like this.</i>

73
00:12:48,273 --> 00:12:49,566
Why the hell do we still do it?

74
00:12:49,608 --> 00:12:52,402
It's our nature to save them.

75
00:12:52,736 --> 00:12:54,196
It's what we do.

76
00:12:54,237 --> 00:12:55,780
Right.

77
00:12:55,822 --> 00:12:58,450
Cherish your life.

78
00:12:58,492 --> 00:12:59,284
What

79
00:12:59,326 --> 00:13:00,243
the fuckin' motto.

80
00:13:00,285 --> 00:13:02,204
We're supposed to cherish our lives.

81
00:13:03,455 --> 00:13:06,458
Well, how the hell are we supposed
to do that when this is out life?

82
00:13:12,005 --> 00:13:13,131
We chose this.

83
00:13:13,798 --> 00:13:14,633
You go home.

84
00:13:14,716 --> 00:13:16,218
<i>Hoffman,</i>
<i>there's two Agents here to see you.</i>

85
00:13:16,259 --> 00:13:17,636
Copy.

86
00:13:20,889 --> 00:13:22,724
-Detective Hoffman?
-<i>Yeah?</i>

87
00:13:23,183 --> 00:13:26,937
I'm Special Agent Lindsey Perez.
This is Special Agent Peter Strahm.

88
00:13:27,854 --> 00:13:29,314
How can I help the FBI?

89
00:13:29,606 --> 00:13:31,566
We're here about detective Kerry.

90
00:13:31,608 --> 00:13:32,692
She was our liaison.

91
00:13:32,734 --> 00:13:34,361
<i>Open</i>
<i>the door and you will find me.</i>

92
00:13:34,778 --> 00:13:35,737
What?

93
00:13:41,993 --> 00:13:42,869
What's this?

94
00:13:42,953 --> 00:13:45,247
The key that came with our last
message from detective Kerry.

95
00:13:45,330 --> 00:13:48,041
"Open the door and you will
find me" mean anything to you?

96
00:13:48,124 --> 00:13:49,125
No.

97
00:13:58,218 --> 00:13:59,511
Where's the body?

98
00:13:59,761 --> 00:14:03,640
The crime scene photographer's flash
picked up this bullet casing.

99
00:14:03,682 --> 00:14:06,059
It was lodged between
the body and the device.

100
00:14:06,101 --> 00:14:07,227
Run it for prints.

101
00:14:14,818 --> 00:14:17,153
Give us the room
a minute, would you? Thanks.

102
00:14:23,493 --> 00:14:24,995
The lock was open.

103
00:14:25,287 --> 00:14:26,413
<i>She couldn't get out.</i>

104
00:14:26,621 --> 00:14:29,165
It was constructed for her execution.

105
00:14:29,583 --> 00:14:30,750
<i>Betrayed the rules.</i>

106
00:14:30,792 --> 00:14:32,252
Not a Jigsaw trap then?

107
00:14:32,335 --> 00:14:33,336
No.

108
00:14:33,628 --> 00:14:35,046
Amanda Young, the accomplice.

109
00:14:35,088 --> 00:14:36,548
This wasn't done by Amanda Young.

110
00:14:36,631 --> 00:14:37,674
Excuse me?

111
00:14:37,757 --> 00:14:40,093
Detective Kerry weighed
approximately 130 pounds.

112
00:14:40,176 --> 00:14:42,137
Amanda Young's
arrest report has her at 107.

113
00:14:42,178 --> 00:14:43,763
She couldn't get her up there alone.

114
00:14:43,805 --> 00:14:44,598
John Kramer was--

115
00:14:44,639 --> 00:14:46,683
That bedridden cancer patient?
He's brains, not brawn.

116
00:14:46,766 --> 00:14:47,934
He was also an engineer.

117
00:14:48,018 --> 00:14:51,187
-<i>He could have Rigged pulleys or--</i>
-Or someone else could have helped him.

118
00:14:51,271 --> 00:14:54,024
Special Agent,
if you're here for any other reason

119
00:14:54,065 --> 00:14:55,275
than just to assist--

120
00:14:55,317 --> 00:14:57,902
We're here to find the person
your department couldn't, detective.

121
00:14:57,944 --> 00:14:59,738
The one helping Jigsaw and Amanda Young.

122
00:15:00,447 --> 00:15:01,865
Excuse me.

123
00:15:08,747 --> 00:15:11,041
We found a harlequin
doll in your possession.

124
00:15:11,082 --> 00:15:12,292
What's that about?

125
00:15:12,334 --> 00:15:16,421
It's a toy. Kids play
with toys, that's all it is.

126
00:15:16,463 --> 00:15:19,424
How about the tricycle

127
00:15:19,883 --> 00:15:22,010
the tricycle is from John's youth.

128
00:15:22,052 --> 00:15:24,554
<i>A grown man a tricycle his whole life?</i>

129
00:15:24,596 --> 00:15:28,350
I'm sure you've kept
things that were important to you.

130
00:15:28,391 --> 00:15:29,809
Look, Mrs. Tuck.

131
00:15:29,851 --> 00:15:33,313
Is there any reason we should
be concerned for your safety?

132
00:15:33,355 --> 00:15:35,607
Perhaps you should be
more concerned for yourself.

133
00:15:35,649 --> 00:15:38,276
Why don't you tell me
everything you know about John

134
00:15:38,318 --> 00:15:39,653
and let's start at the beginning.

135
00:15:39,694 --> 00:15:43,323
John's life defies
chronology and linear description.

136
00:15:43,365 --> 00:15:45,200
So why don't we start at the end

137
00:15:45,241 --> 00:15:47,160
and let's work our way backwards.

138
00:15:47,202 --> 00:15:49,496
I represent Mrs. Tuck.

139
00:15:51,331 --> 00:15:52,582
She knows something.

140
00:15:52,624 --> 00:15:54,751
I thought you were going home.

141
00:15:54,793 --> 00:15:56,419
You have vacation time, right?

142
00:15:56,461 --> 00:15:59,506
Take it. Finish the remodeling

143
00:15:59,547 --> 00:16:01,257
spend some time with tracy.

144
00:16:01,299 --> 00:16:02,342
She understands.

145
00:16:02,384 --> 00:16:04,386
Then don't take her for granted.

146
00:16:04,678 --> 00:16:06,471
Eric is still out there, man.

147
00:16:06,513 --> 00:16:07,931
Eric's been missing for 6 months.

148
00:16:07,972 --> 00:16:09,432
Kerry was gone for 4 days.

149
00:16:09,474 --> 00:16:11,768
I can only be as
optimistic as the facts allow.

150
00:16:11,810 --> 00:16:13,770
Yeah. Well, I'm in it until I find them.

151
00:16:13,812 --> 00:16:15,438
Finding his body
isn't going to vindicate us.

152
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:17,524
Finding him alive will.

153
00:16:17,565 --> 00:16:19,109
It's time to let go.

154
00:16:19,150 --> 00:16:20,360
I want you to go home.

155
00:16:20,402 --> 00:16:25,448
I'll call you later to
make sure everything is ok.

156
00:16:29,494 --> 00:16:30,495
Who's he?

157
00:16:30,537 --> 00:16:32,580
Lieutenant Rigg, our swat commander.

158
00:16:32,622 --> 00:16:33,665
What's his problem?

159
00:16:33,707 --> 00:16:36,459
Everyone around him keeps dying.

160
00:16:57,021 --> 00:16:58,565
What's it say?

161
00:16:58,606 --> 00:17:02,485
It says I tried calling you 4 times.

162
00:17:02,527 --> 00:17:06,573
It says dinner is in the fridge.

163
00:17:06,614 --> 00:17:09,784
And at the bottom it says I love you.

164
00:17:09,826 --> 00:17:14,622
I need to help my mom for a few days.

165
00:17:14,664 --> 00:17:18,460
Just come with me.

166
00:17:18,501 --> 00:17:19,794
Ok? Now.

167
00:17:19,836 --> 00:17:22,547
I can't.

168
00:17:23,256 --> 00:17:24,841
You can...

169
00:17:24,883 --> 00:17:27,260
but you won't.

170
00:17:27,594 --> 00:17:33,516
What you can't do is save everyone.

171
00:17:42,192 --> 00:17:43,651
Tracy?

172
00:17:43,693 --> 00:17:46,696
Tracy, please, listen to me.

173
00:17:58,666 --> 00:18:03,630
John Kramer owned a company
called "the urban renewal group."

174
00:18:03,671 --> 00:18:05,465
No irony in that, huh?

175
00:18:05,507 --> 00:18:06,758
What was Rigg watching?

176
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,384
Jill tuck's interrogation.

177
00:18:08,426 --> 00:18:10,595
She was Jigsaw's ex. It's old.

178
00:18:10,637 --> 00:18:13,139
Why is a swat guy watching that?

179
00:18:13,181 --> 00:18:14,140
Strahm...

180
00:18:14,182 --> 00:18:16,476
I really think we should tell Hoffman

181
00:18:16,518 --> 00:18:18,603
what detective Kerry
said in her last message.

182
00:18:18,645 --> 00:18:21,105
She said two Officers might be in danger,

183
00:18:21,147 --> 00:18:23,691
but until we know
who we're not causing a panic.

184
00:18:23,733 --> 00:18:25,944
If detective Hoffman or
anyone else in this precinct

185
00:18:25,985 --> 00:18:27,779
is in danger, I think they should know it.

186
00:18:27,821 --> 00:18:29,656
Not your call.

187
00:18:33,451 --> 00:18:35,411
Making any progress?

188
00:18:36,329 --> 00:18:38,373
We're fine, thanks.

189
00:18:38,623 --> 00:18:40,416
Hey, boss. It looks like another doctor

190
00:18:40,458 --> 00:18:41,501
went missing from the hospital.

191
00:18:41,543 --> 00:18:42,585
They think maybe it's a...

192
00:18:42,627 --> 00:18:45,213
Thanks. I'll check it out.

193
00:18:45,255 --> 00:18:46,548
If you need me, call my cell.

194
00:18:46,589 --> 00:18:48,675
The coffee machine's around the corner.

195
00:18:48,716 --> 00:18:50,593
-Boy or girl?
-Girl.

196
00:18:50,927 --> 00:18:52,470
I didn't know you were married.

197
00:18:52,512 --> 00:18:54,097
I'm not. It's a short story, believe me.

198
00:19:12,407 --> 00:19:14,117
Tracy?

199
00:19:29,799 --> 00:19:30,842
Tracy?

200
00:20:19,307 --> 00:20:21,684
Uhh!

201
00:20:39,702 --> 00:20:40,578
<i>Yeah?</i>

202
00:20:40,620 --> 00:20:42,497
We pulled a print off that casing.

203
00:20:43,373 --> 00:20:44,540
We got a match.

204
00:20:44,916 --> 00:20:48,503
-Jesus. You check this?
-Twice.

205
00:20:57,303 --> 00:20:58,262
Ah!

206
00:21:26,874 --> 00:21:27,959
Shit.

207
00:21:28,334 --> 00:21:31,170
Hello, Officer Rigg.
Welcome to your rebirth.

208
00:21:31,212 --> 00:21:35,008
For years you have
stood by and have witnessed

209
00:21:35,049 --> 00:21:37,677
<i>as your colleagues have fallen.</i>

210
00:21:37,719 --> 00:21:39,846
You have remained untouched,

211
00:21:39,887 --> 00:21:41,931
while Eric Matthew has disappeared.

212
00:21:41,973 --> 00:21:44,892
<i>But with your survival</i>
<i>came your obsession.</i>

213
00:21:44,934 --> 00:21:49,355
Obsession to stop those around
you from making the wrong choices.

214
00:21:49,397 --> 00:21:52,775
Thus preventing
you from making the right ones.

215
00:21:52,817 --> 00:21:54,193
You wanted to save everyone,

216
00:21:54,235 --> 00:21:58,364
tonight I give you the opportunity
to face your obsession.

217
00:21:58,406 --> 00:22:03,494
Look closely.
Eric Matthews is still alive.

218
00:22:03,536 --> 00:22:07,457
The block of ice
he stands upon is melting.

219
00:22:07,498 --> 00:22:10,043
He has but 90 minutes to save himself.

220
00:22:10,084 --> 00:22:15,214
Detective Hoffman's
fate is linked to eric's survival.

221
00:22:15,256 --> 00:22:17,842
Heed my warning, Officer Rigg.

222
00:22:17,884 --> 00:22:21,846
Their lives hang in
the balance of your obsession.

223
00:22:21,888 --> 00:22:26,225
Will you learn how to
let go and truly save them?

224
00:22:26,267 --> 00:22:29,771
The choice is yours.

225
00:23:19,070 --> 00:23:20,029
Jesus!

226
00:23:22,657 --> 00:23:24,200
Take off the mask,
put your hands in the air!

227
00:23:24,283 --> 00:23:25,493
I can't!

228
00:23:25,701 --> 00:23:26,619
Help!

229
00:23:39,048 --> 00:23:40,758
Officer Rigg. Your first test.

230
00:23:40,800 --> 00:23:44,595
The person in front of
you is in desperate need of help.

231
00:23:44,637 --> 00:23:46,889
But it is not your job to save them.

232
00:23:46,931 --> 00:23:48,850
<i>For you this person is a victim.</i>

233
00:23:48,891 --> 00:23:51,269
<i>But if you were to see what I see</i>

234
00:23:51,310 --> 00:23:56,732
<i>beneath the mask lies a criminal</i>
<i>undeserving of the life she leads.</i>

235
00:24:00,820 --> 00:24:01,904
Get me out of here!

236
00:24:02,488 --> 00:24:05,241
<i>Your obsession tells</i>
<i>you to save the victim.</i>

237
00:24:05,324 --> 00:24:07,243
I tell you to walk away.

238
00:24:07,326 --> 00:24:08,703
The choice is yours.

239
00:24:11,038 --> 00:24:12,123
Are you a cop?

240
00:24:12,165 --> 00:24:13,457
-What?
-Are you a cop?!

241
00:24:13,541 --> 00:24:14,375
Yeah, I'm a cop.

242
00:24:19,046 --> 00:24:21,883
<i>What is that? What is that?</i>

243
00:24:27,805 --> 00:24:31,309
Help! Help! They're in the gears!

244
00:24:31,350 --> 00:24:35,855
-What's in the gears?
-The combination. Get me out!

245
00:24:37,690 --> 00:24:40,359
Cut my hair! Just get me out! Cut my hair!

246
00:24:40,401 --> 00:24:41,861
-Just relax!
-Hurry!

247
00:24:43,446 --> 00:24:45,323
Get me out of here, please!

248
00:24:45,406 --> 00:24:46,949
Aah! Get me out!

249
00:24:47,033 --> 00:24:48,451
Aah! Aah!

250
00:24:49,535 --> 00:24:51,495
Please! Where are you going?

251
00:24:51,704 --> 00:24:54,207
<i>Wait! Wait! Please, wait! Wait!</i>

252
00:24:54,332 --> 00:24:56,292
<i>Please! Please!</i>

253
00:24:56,334 --> 00:24:57,501
-Shit.
-<i>Wait!</i>

254
00:24:58,044 --> 00:25:01,172
Stop! Aah!

255
00:25:01,214 --> 00:25:02,298
Fucking cut me out!

256
00:25:02,340 --> 00:25:05,718
I'm sorry, I'm sorry. Please come back.

257
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:07,053
Please come back.

258
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:29,951
Where the hell is the combination? Shit!

259
00:25:39,502 --> 00:25:40,586
I got one!

260
00:25:40,670 --> 00:25:42,296
I got one! Hold on!

261
00:25:42,338 --> 00:25:44,006
