01:23:31,178 --> 01:23:33,055
Will you learn how to let go?

1023
01:23:34,265 --> 01:23:35,683
Eric is still out there, man.

1024
01:23:35,725 --> 01:23:36,684
It's time to let go.

1025
01:23:36,726 --> 01:23:39,311
Detective Matthews has but 90 minutes.

1026
01:23:39,353 --> 01:23:41,480
I recommend you stay alive

1027
01:23:41,522 --> 01:23:43,816
until the fucking clock counts down.

1028
01:23:43,858 --> 01:23:46,235
They had to save themselves.

1029
01:23:46,277 --> 01:23:48,237
Aah! Take them!

1030
01:23:50,656 --> 01:23:54,368
<i>Their salvation was out of your hands.</i>

1031
01:23:54,410 --> 01:23:55,244
Aah!

1032
01:23:55,286 --> 01:23:56,287
Time was on your side,

1033
01:23:56,328 --> 01:23:58,998
but your obsession wouldn't let you wait.

1034
01:23:59,039 --> 01:24:02,209
Instead of saving detective Matthews,

1035
01:24:02,251 --> 01:24:04,253
you cost him his life.

1036
01:24:04,295 --> 01:24:07,590
You failed your final test.

1037
01:24:30,780 --> 01:24:32,239
What I don't understand is...

1038
01:24:32,281 --> 01:24:33,699
how the hell could Jigsaw do all of this?

1039
01:24:33,741 --> 01:24:36,243
He was damn near on his deathbed
the last time we saw him.

1040
01:24:36,285 --> 01:24:37,745
I'm not so sure he did.

1041
01:24:44,251 --> 01:24:46,253
This wasn't done by Amanda Young.

1042
01:24:46,295 --> 01:24:47,213
Excuse me?

1043
01:24:47,254 --> 01:24:48,297
She couldn't get her up there alone.

1044
01:24:48,339 --> 01:24:49,882
-John Kramer was--
-He's brains, not brawn.

1045
01:24:50,382 --> 01:24:54,053
We're here to find the person
helping Jigsaw and Amanda Young.

1046
01:25:03,395 --> 01:25:06,565
Looks like another doctor
went missing from the hospital.

1047
01:25:07,358 --> 01:25:09,985
Aah!

1048
01:25:10,069 --> 01:25:11,362
You go home.

1049
01:25:14,865 --> 01:25:17,201
You chose this.

1050
01:25:33,259 --> 01:25:34,510
Game over.

1051
01:26:03,122 --> 01:26:06,000
<i>You feel</i>
<i>you now have control, don't you?</i>

1052
01:26:07,585 --> 01:26:10,462
You think you will walk away untested.

1053
01:26:17,428 --> 01:26:20,723
<i>I promise that my work will continue.</i>

1054
01:26:21,724 --> 01:26:23,726
<i>That I have ensured.</i>

1055
01:26:24,226 --> 01:26:28,647
<i>By hearing this tape,</i>
<i>some will assume that this is over.</i>

1056
01:26:28,689 --> 01:26:30,524
<i>But I am still among you.</i>

1057
01:26:31,775 --> 01:26:35,571
<i>You think it's over just because I'm dead?</i>

1058
01:26:35,613 --> 01:26:37,281
<i>It's not over.</i>

1059
01:26:37,323 --> 01:26:39,617
<i>The games have just begun.</i>

1060
01:31:19,980 --> 01:31:22,774
Captioning made
possible by lions gate entertainment

1061
